    "description": "Add the records-commit-trailer input\n\nA consumer whose deployment platform builds every branch of its repo gets a failed build on every push to `pr-review-records`, because that branch holds only records. In `jerridan/websites`, both Vercel projects fail on each review with \"The specified Root Directory does not exist\".\n\nThis adds one optional input to the reusable workflow, `records-commit-trailer`. The commit step appends it to the records commit message. A Vercel consumer passes `[vercel skip]`, and Vercel then skips the records branch. The default is empty, so every other consumer's commit message is unchanged, byte for byte.\n\nThe input reaches the script through `env`, as the file's rules require. Two tests cover the step: the default message, and the message with the trailer. The README documents the input under \"The records branch\".\n\nAfter merge, move `v1` to the new commit and bump the SHA pin in `jerridan/websites`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015qFsP83RdSgDuy1Cj27jH6",
